\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Does the Kobayashi pseudometric vanish identically on every compact Calabi–Yau manifold? In particular, must every such manifold be Kobayashi non-hyperbolic and contain an entire curve?
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2017/39}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Does the Kobayashi pseudometric vanish identically on every compact Calabi–Yau manifold? In particular, must every such manifold be Kobayashi non-hyperbolic and contain an entire curve?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 30003573 (OWR-15582-007). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2017/39}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:30003573}

